  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nMainly dry conditions are expected to continue through the remainder \nof the week and beginning of the weekend. High pressure over the \nOhio Valley and Lower Great Lakes will exit to the east as a cold \nfront swings southeast across the region Wednesday evening. Most of \nthe forecast area will remain dry with the frontal passage outside \nof low-end PoPs in lake enhanced rain showers across Northwest \nPennsylvania Wednesday night. \n\nAnother area of high pressure builds overhead behind the cold front \nwhich will continue the prolonged dry conditions through early\nSunday. By Sunday, a disturbance originating from the Gulf will\nmove north towards the Tennessee and Ohio Valleys bringing \nincreased tropical moisture to the region. If the forecasted \ntrack persists, widespread rainfall is expected Sunday into \nMonday. Will continue to monitor forecast trends with this \ndisturbance in the coming days. \n\nHigh temperature through the period will generally remain in the \nupper 60s to lower 70s. Slightly warmer highs possible Wednesday and \nSaturday in the mid 70s as a warm front will lift across the \nregion both days.",
